{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:288fa8c94995665b","name":"AT-CT","source":{"id":"source:reference-288fa8c94995665b","title":"AT-CT","revision":15630,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:52:57Z","sha256":"2329537541817b91b540615cb15d42e9e34eee2cd7ef65d7aee70b646ed380ec","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15630","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=AT-CT&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-288fa8c94995665b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For large-scale construction projects on distant worlds, many Imperial engineers have adapted the ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-ST"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-ST","referenceId":"reference:42d3fc5263e8fdb5"}," frame to produce a Vehicle capable of assisting in the construction of new facilities. Using advanced ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beam","referenceId":"reference:627f44a03c76e65b"}," technology, these All Terrain Construction Transports (as the variant is commonly known) can lift, manipulate, and move unattended objects at range, effectively allowing them to place girders, crates, and other pieces of heavy equipment exactly where construction crews need them.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In order to maintain this fine level of control over the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beams"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beams"},", all other weapons and extraneous systems had to be stripped out of the Walker, leaving it unarmed. AT-CT pilots quickly learned to defend themselves against attacks, using the AT-CT's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beams"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beams"}," to hurl objects at their targets.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If an AT-CT has successfully ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grabbed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grabbed"}," an object with its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beam","referenceId":"reference:627f44a03c76e65b"},", it can move the object up to 10 squares in any direction (instead of being limited to bringing the object closer). Additionally, an AT-CT can hurl a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grabbed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grabbed"}," object at another target within 10 squares, making a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranged Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranged_Attack"}," using the Tractor Beam's attack bonus. If the attack roll exceeds the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},", the target takes damage based on the size of the object being hurled (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Falling Objects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Falling_Objects"},").\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Expert)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["AT-CT Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Walker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walker"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 1